{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 (29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8) recorded 18 below-seam ambient config/credential reads in the store/snapshot/io subsystem (_store, _snapshot, _io) as `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`. RP-04 is not complete while these sit below the seams enforced by `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent: 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab.\n\nThe 18 flagged reads: 3 `load_config()` (_store/ensures.py:245, _store/project_ensures.py:69, _store/push.py:63); env reads REBAR_SNAPSHOT_STALL_{ATTEMPTS,WINDOW_SECONDS,FLOOR_BYTES_PER_SEC} (git_fetch.py), REBAR_GATE_{FREE_WATERMARK_BYTES,GRACE_SECONDS,JANITOR_INTERVAL_SECONDS,MAX_AGE_SECONDS,REVERIFY_SECONDS} + a dynamic os.environ.get (janitor.py L73), REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR (repo_snapshot.py), REBAR_ALLOW_ENV_REIDENTIFY (env_identity.py), REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES (lock.py), REBAR_HLC + REBAR_HLC_NOW (hlc.py), REBAR_SYNC_PUSH (import_ndjson.py L216/217/395).\n\nAffected SOURCE files: the 10 above plus `src/rebar/config.py` (adds/reuses owned resolvers) and `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py` (removes the 18 rows).\n\nAffected TEST consumers (updated in-scope — they set the cut env vars directly and drive the affected helpers): `tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py`, `test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4.py`, `test_network_fetch_stall_abort_851e.py`, `test_repo_snapshot.py`, `test_snapshot_cache.py`, `test_snapshot_blobless_747f.py`, `test_snapshot_docs.py`, `test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py`, and any test setting `REBAR_ALLOW_ENV_REIDENTIFY` driving `_store/env_identity.py`.\n\n## Outcome\nEach of the 18 reads is dispositioned by the decision rule into exactly one treatment and its `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` row removed. `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` reports zero findings for these paths, no path-glob exception. Regression suites (below) stay green, including the REBAR_SYNC_PUSH import-defer coupling. Redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes unchanged except recorded deltas (comment on this ticket).\n\n## Decision rule\n- **(a) CUT-TO-SEAM (default; majority).** A read whose value is composed config is CUT: routed through an owned `config.py` resolver instead of ambient `os.environ`/`load_config` below the seam; the ambient read no longer exists. Below-seam helper signatures change to RECEIVE the value, so the `tests/unit` consumers inject via the new signature/typed config and run in the regression suite. **Preserve resolution timing:** a read resolved live per operation is cut to a resolver that itself reads live per call (see push.py coupling), NOT composed once and threaded — otherwise a mid-operation override is silently lost.\n- **(b) OWNED-IN-PLACE via `# read-via:` marker (bounded allowlist ONLY).** A read that is NOT composed config — genuine test-only injection, subsystem kill-switch, or subprocess/protocol env-control — stays with a `# read-via:` marker naming the category. CAPPED at the 3 enumerated logical reads below; the gate flags each accessed LINE separately, so those 3 reads = exactly **5 marked lines**. No other listed read may be marked.\n\n### Owned-in-place allowlist (3 reads = 5 marked lines — the cap)\n1. `_store/hlc.py` L61 `REBAR_HLC` — subsystem kill-switch (`REBAR_HLC=0` reverts HLC to raw `physical_now()`). 1 line.\n2. `_store/hlc.py` L71 `REBAR_HLC_NOW` — test-only injection of the physical clock source. 1 line.\n3. `_io/import_ndjson.py` L216/L217/L395 `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH` — subprocess/protocol env-control: L216 reads prior value, L217 sets `=off` (defer per-event push during bulk import), L395 restores. Not composed config. 3 lines.\n\nAll 15 other reads are treatment (a).\n\n## The push.py / import_ndjson coupling (must stay correct)\n`push.py:63` resolves `sync.push` **live per push**, and `import_ndjson` sets `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off` in the process env precisely so those live reads defer per-event pushes during a bulk import, then restores and does one final push. Cutting push.py to a value composed once at the seam would stop it observing that mutation and break import push-deferral. Resolution: cut push.py:63 to an owned `config.py` resolver `resolve_push_mode(root)` that resolves **live per call** (env>config>`always` default, wrapping `normalize_push_mode`); push.py's `_push_mode` keeps its `current_push_mode()` startup-binding precedence then calls the live resolver. import_ndjson's `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH` env-control stays owned-in-place (b) and continues to drive that live resolver. Same live-per-call rule applies to any other live-resolved read among the cuts.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add/confirm owned `config.py` resolvers (reuse `compose_config()`; add `resolve_push_mode(root)` live resolver; add narrow typed resolvers where cleaner). Cut the 15 composed-config reads to route through them, changing below-seam helper signatures to RECEIVE the value. Preserve exact semantics (env>config>default for `[snapshot]` knobs; clamping for `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES`; live-per-call for push mode).\n2. Update the affected `tests/unit` consumers to inject via the new signature/typed config; keep their assertions.\n3. Mark the 3 owned-in-place reads (5 lines) with `# read-via:` markers naming the category; no other markers.\n4. Remove the 18 rows from `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS`.\n5. Run `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and the regression set; keep green.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\nHeld-out `tests/scripts/test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py` asserts: (i) `check_config_ownership.check(REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding containing any listed source path; (ii) `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` has zero entries whose `path` is a listed source file; (iii) `# read-via:` markers across the listed source files total exactly 5, confined to `_store/hlc.py` (2) and `_io/import_ndjson.py` (3) — every other listed file has 0 — so blanket-marking cannot substitute for cutting. RED now.\nCoupling regression (held-out): a bulk `import_ndjson` run with N interior writes and `sync.push=always` performs exactly ONE push (proving the cut `resolve_push_mode` still observes the mid-import `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off` env mutation); RED if push.py is cut to a compose-once value.\nRegression suites kept green: `tests/interfaces/store`, `tests/integration` store/snapshot, AND the affected `tests/unit` suites listed above. Redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints before/after equal except recorded deltas.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nNo stored format changes. Cut-to-seam is routing/threading; the 5 marked lines are inline annotations on 3 non-config env-control reads. Rollback = revert the single change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No ambient config/credential read, backend reload, or configurable default remains below the seam in the 10 listed source files: each read is cut-to-seam (15) or one of the 3 enumerated owned-in-place reads (5 marked lines) with a `# read-via:` rationale; no other read marked; live-resolved reads (push mode) cut to a live-per-call resolver, not a compose-once value.\n- [x] The 18 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows are removed and `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out test incl. its marker-total==5 / per-file-placement check).\n- [x] The regression suites in Testing pass after the cutover, including the REBAR_SYNC_PUSH import-defer coupling test; operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes unchanged except deltas recorded with rationale as a comment on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787112098329074001,"uuid":"f01b4a52-624e-45b1-8a98-d223d7322b2b"}